Question 10 : Constructor + Field Initialization + Overriding
class A {

    A() {
        print();
    }

    void print() {
        System.out.println("A");
    }
}

class B extends A {

    int x = 5;

    void print() {
        System.out.println(x);
    }
}

public class Main {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        B b = new B();

        b.print();
    }
}


======================================output===========================================

Parent constructor runs.

A() {
    print();
}

Calls overridden method.

So:

B.print()

executes.

At this moment:

int x = 5;

has not initialized yet.

Default value:

x = 0

First output:

0
Step 2

Parent constructor finishes.

Step 3

Field initialization happens.

x = 5
Step 4

Main:
b.print();

Now x is initialized.

Output:

5

Final:

0
5
